"```json\n{\n    \"critic_suggestions\": \"1. Severe Node Overlaps: Multiple nodes significantly collide and overlap due to insufficient horizontal and vertical node spacing:\\n   - The 'Fixed baseline' box directly overlaps the top-right of the 'Observations' box, obscuring the title and border.\\n   - The scalar correction box ($b = \\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\sum r_i = 3$) collides with and covers the right portion of the 'Residuals' box.\\n   - The 'Evaluation' box overlaps the right side of the 'Corrected prediction' box, truncating its label to 'Corrected predictio...'.\\n   Enlarge horizontal canvas spacing (or reduce node padding/width) so that each stage occupies a dedicated horizontal column with clear margins.\\n2. Text Formatting & Hyphenation: In the Evaluation block, awkward automatic line wrapping causes hyphenations ('arith-metic', 'gener-alization') and splits mathematical expressions ($e_i = \\\\hat{y}_i -$ on one line and $y_i = 0$ on the next). Widen the evaluation block slightly to allow clean line breaks without mid-word or mid-formula hyphens.\\n3. Arrow Routing and Clarity:\\n   - The arrow from Observations ($x$) to Fixed baseline loops awkwardly over the top; position Fixed baseline cleanly to the right of Observations to allow a natural, direct arrow.\\n   - The connection from Corrected prediction to Evaluation loops awkwardly at the top border due to overlapping bounding boxes. A clean, horizontal arrow should connect the right edge of Corrected prediction directly to the left edge of Evaluation.\",\n    \"revised_description\": \"**Figure description: `fig_residual_workflow` (diagram, LaTeX/TikZ)**\\n\\n**Canvas and style**\\n- Pure white background, no border, no drop shadows, no gradients.\\n- Landscape canvas, dimensions approximately 16 cm \u00d7 7 cm, laid out strictly from left to right across 5 non-overlapping horizontal stages with generous spacing to avoid collisions.\\n- All text and math in Computer Modern: 8\u20139 pt for annotations, 9\u201310 pt for node labels, 10 pt for mathematical symbols.\\n- Rounded rectangular nodes with 3 pt corner radius, 0.6 pt outline, and light thematic fills:\\n  - Observations: pale blue fill `#DDEBF7`, outline `#2F5597`.\\n  - Baseline predictor: light gray fill `#EFEFEF`, outline `#595959`.\\n  - Residuals & scalar correction: pale orange fill `#FBE5D6`, outline `#C55A11`.\\n  - Corrected prediction: pale green fill `#E2F0D9`, outline `#548235`.\\n  - Evaluation: white fill, dark gray outline `#404040`.\\n- Arrows:\\n  - Solid computation/dependency arrows: 0.8 pt line width, dark gray `#333333`, `-Stealth` tips.\\n  - Dashed reuse path: 0.6 pt dashed (3 pt on, 2 pt off), color `#2F5597`, routed along the bottom row.\\n\\n**Layout and elements (strictly non-overlapping, left to right)**\\n\\n1. **Observation block (Column 1, centered vertically)**\\n   - A tall rounded box labeled 'Observations ($n = 5$)' at the top.\\n   - Contains a minimal two-column table:\\n     - Header: $x$ and $y = 2x+3$ separated by a horizontal rule.\\n     - Rows: $(-2, -1), (-1, 1), (0, 3), (1, 5), (2, 7)$.\\n   - Keep width around 3.0 cm so it does not collide with subsequent columns.\\n\\n2. **Baseline predictor (Column 2, upper row)**\\n   - Positioned horizontally to the right of the Observation block (clearing its right border completely by at least 0.8 cm) and vertically aligned above the Residuals block.\\n   - Box labeled 'Fixed baseline' with $\\\\hat{y}^{(0)} = 2x$.\\n   - Direct incoming solid arrow from the $x$ column/anchor of the Observation block to the baseline box, labeled '$x$'.\\n\\n3. **Residual computation (Column 2, lower row)**\\n   - Pale orange box positioned directly below the Baseline predictor box with clear vertical separation.\\n   - Labeled 'Residuals' with formula $r_i = y_i - 2x_i$.\\n   - Displays computed values: $r_i = 3, 3, 3, 3, 3$ ($i=1,\\\\dots,5$).\\n   - Incoming solid arrow from the $y$ column of the Observation block (labeled '$y_i$') and a vertical solid arrow from the Fixed baseline box above (labeled '$2x_i$').\\n\\n4. **Scalar correction (Column 3, vertically centered with Residuals)**\\n   - Pale orange box placed strictly to the right of the Residuals box (clearing it with at least 0.8 cm gap).\\n   - Contains $b = \\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{5} r_i = 3$.\\n   - Incoming horizontal arrow from Residuals to $b$.\\n   - Beneath this arrow, the key annotation: 'data dependency: correction computed from observed residuals' in 8 pt italic text.\\n\\n5. **Corrected prediction (Column 4, vertically centered)**\\n   - Pale green box placed strictly to the right of Column 3.\\n   - Labeled 'Corrected prediction' with formula $\\\\hat{y}_i = 2x_i + b$.\\n   - Incoming arrow 1: A route from the top of the Fixed baseline box running horizontally above the canvas and descending into the top of the Corrected prediction box, labeled '$2x_i$'.\\n   - Incoming arrow 2: Horizontal solid arrow from the scalar correction box $b$ to the left edge of Corrected prediction, labeled '$+b$'.\\n\\n6. **Evaluation block (Column 5, far right, vertically centered)**\\n   - White rounded box placed strictly to the right of Corrected prediction with clear separation (at least 0.8 cm gap).\\n   - Sufficient width (~3.2 cm) to display text cleanly without awkward word breaks:\\n     - Title: 'Evaluation on the same 5 observations'\\n     - Math: $e_i = \\\\hat{y}_i - y_i = 0$ (on a single line)\\n     - Note: 'finite arithmetic check, not generalization' (without hyphenating 'arithmetic' or 'generalization').\\n   - Direct horizontal solid arrow from the right edge of Corrected prediction to the left edge of Evaluation.\\n   - Dashed blue reuse arrow running from the bottom of the Observation block, dropping to a lower corridor below all blocks, and entering the bottom of the Evaluation block. Labeled along the path: 'same observations reused' in 8 pt blue text.\\n\\n**Output format notes**\\n- Native editable `.tex` source ensuring coordinate/node positioning (`right=of ...`, `above=of ...`) prevents node overlaps.\\n- Vector PDF and 300 dpi raster preview.\"\n}\n```"